  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="DA">IWGIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DA">The project aims at engaging students from Danish Universities on issues related to the 
rights of Indigenous Peoples, providing them with a perspective relevant to their 
studies not addressed in traditional curricula in Denmark. The project will offer a oneweek-course for up to 35 students on issues such as international mechanisms, land rights and human rights defenders. The project will also propose internships for up to 8 Danish students with IWGIA&#x2019;s partner organisations to experience the realities behind the theories and get close to the issues dealt with in the course. During their internship, the students will be required to produce audiovisual materials to engage students in Denmark in a reflexion on SDGs 1, 4, 10, 15 and 16.</narrative>
  </description>
